1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,366
Disney is famous

2
00:00:01,366 --> 00:00:02,720
for its movies.

3
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:04,600
But its profit comes

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,370
from somewhere else.

5
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:07,675
In nine months,

6
00:00:07,675 --> 00:00:08,574
Disney made

7
00:00:08,574 --> 00:00:11,147
$14.8 billion in

8
00:00:11,147 --> 00:00:13,000
operating income.

9
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,786
61% of it came

10
00:00:14,786 --> 00:00:16,592
from one division:

11
00:00:16,592 --> 00:00:17,745
Experiences.

12
00:00:17,745 --> 00:00:18,625
Theme parks,

13
00:00:18,625 --> 00:00:19,520
resorts,

14
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,316
cruises and

15
00:00:20,316 --> 00:00:21,660
merchandise.

16
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:22,505
Movies,

17
00:00:22,505 --> 00:00:24,100
TV and Disney Plus?

18
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,060
Just 28%.

19
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:27,690
Sports made the rest.

20
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:28,696
Yet entertainment

21
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:30,350
brings in more revenue:

22
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:32,163
$34.7 billion,

23
00:00:32,163 --> 00:00:34,770
against $29.5 billion.

24
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:35,762
On each dollar

25
00:00:35,762 --> 00:00:36,600
of sales,

26
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,856
Experiences kept 30¢.

27
00:00:38,856 --> 00:00:39,728
Entertainment

28
00:00:39,728 --> 00:00:40,870
kept 12¢.

29
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:41,910
Last quarter,

30
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:43,655
attendance at Disney's

31
00:00:43,655 --> 00:00:45,770
US parks rose 3%,

32
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:46,661
and each guest

33
00:00:46,661 --> 00:00:48,610
spent 4% more.

34
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:49,403
Disney makes

35
00:00:49,403 --> 00:00:50,330
the movies.

36
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:51,024
The parks make

37
00:00:51,024 --> 00:00:51,920
the money.

38
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,070
More on the channel.
